> Why does the getCurrentRefinements returns something that looks like a promise?

So all the utils are just returning the global "browser" variable created by webdriver.io, it represents the currently opened browser and you access all the API methods from http://webdriver.io/api.html

But it's also a sort of magic promise chain so that after each command you can use .then() to check the results.

> How does getCurrentRefinements get the state?

Here's the implementation:

```js
export function getCurrentRefinements() {
  return browser
    .element('#current-refined-values .item')
    .then(() => browser
      .getText('#current-refined-values .item')
      .then(res => {
        return res.map(refinement => {
          const data = refinement.split('\n');
          const out = {
            name: data[0]
          };

          if (data[1] !== undefined) {
            out.count = parseInt(data[1], 10);
          }

          return out;
        });
      })
    )
    .catch(() => Promise.resolve([]));
}
```

So it's pretty raw but does the job.

